    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p>觸鬚怪看起來像是一個長着寬大尖利鳥喙的氣球狀漂浮大腦。在它堅硬的纖維狀硬皮鞘中包裹着數以百計的環狀肌肉，組成了十根長長的觸鬚。每根觸鬚的末端則是用來注射麻痹毒藥的尖刺。觸鬚怪能夠暫時收起尖刺以方便自己操作那些它不想刺穿或者扯壞的物件。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">觸鬚怪依靠某種浮力使自己漂浮在空中。它們沒有眼睛，但具有敏銳的聽力，以及對震動和電場敏感的皮膚。觸鬚怪可以依此偵測身邊的生物或其他物件。而這種利用電場移動和感知的能力同樣使觸鬚怪能夠吸收閃電而不受其傷害。<br />觸鬚怪天性喜獨居，但偶爾也會聚在一起組成集會coven。</p><p><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>浮游伏擊者Floating Ambushers。</strong></em>觸鬚怪偏好伏擊落單或離羣的生物。它們靜靜的漂浮在通道或者洞窟頂部等待着合適的獵物出現。一旦發現獵物，觸鬚怪便會迅速下降並用它的觸鬚包裹住獵物，然後帶着被抓住的&amp;Reference[condition=paralyzed]{麻痹}生物飄回自己的巢穴。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>異形吞食者Alien Devourers。</strong></em>觸鬚怪是一種怪異的獵食者，它將其他生物分爲三類：能喫、不能喫和大喫貨Great Eater（某些可能會把觸鬚怪視爲獵物的罕見生物）。觸鬚怪在襲擊那些“能喫”的生物是（包括類人生物）不帶一絲憐憫。卻會主動避開那些體型過大自己沒法搬動的生物。</p><p>觸鬚怪有時會旁觀冒險者與其他地下城居民的戰鬥，儘可能不和那些看起來威脅更大的冒險者發生衝突，但仍會伺機發動攻擊。</p><p><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">“隊裏勇敢的遊蕩者爬上了通風井去綁好繩子。一聲喘息過後，繩子便掉了下來。我們從此再也沒見過她。”</em></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:right;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan;text-align:right\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">某冒險者敘述他們在吉波爾Khyber遇到一隻觸鬚怪的攻擊，摘自《科倫堡編年史Korranberg Chronicle》</em></p><p>A grell resembles a bulbous floating brain with a wide, sharp beak. Its ten long tentacles are made of hundreds of ring-shaped muscles sheathed in tough fibrous hide. Sharp barbs line the tip each tentacle and inject paralytic venom. The grell can partially retract its barbs into its tentacles to handle or manipulate objects it doesn't want to pierce or tear.</p><p>Grells have no eyes and floats by means of a sort of levitation. They have keen hearing, however, and their skin is sensitive to vibrations and electrical fields, allowing them to detect the presence of creatures and objects in their immediate vicinity. The creature's ability to manipulate electricity to sense and move also allow it to absorb lightning without harm.</p><p>Although solitary by nature, grells sometimes gather in small groups called covens.</p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Floating Ambushers\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Floating Ambushers.</span> A grell prefers to ambush lone creatures or stragglers, hovering silently near the ceiling of a passage or cavern until a suitable target passes below, whereupon it descends quickly and wraps its tentacles around its prey. It then floats away to its lair with the &amp;Reference[condition=paralyzed] creature in its clutches.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Alien Devourers\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Alien Devourers.</span> Grell are alien predators that group other creatures into three categories: edibles, inedibles, and Great Eaters (those rare creatures that might prey on a grell). Grells have no compunction about attacking creatures they classify as edible, including humanoids. They tend to avoid bigger creatures that they have little hope of carrying away.</p><p>A grell will sometimes allow adventurers to wage war on the other monstrous inhabitants of the dungeon complex it calls home, staying out of the adventurers' way as they dispose of larger threats while waiting for the right time to strike.</p></div></div><div class=\"rd__b-special rd__b-inset rd__b-inset--readaloud\"><div class=\"rd__quote\"><p class=\"rd__quote-line rd__quote-line--last\">“<em>Our intrepid rogue climbed up the shaft to secure a rope. There was a gasp, and the rope fell. We never saw her again.</em>”</p><p><span class=\"rd__quote-by\">— An adventurer's account of a grell attack in Khyber, published in </span><span class=\"small-caps\">The Korranberg Chronicle</span></p></div></div></div>",
        "public": ""
      },
